# CODEOWNERS for <PROJECT_NAME>
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Patterns are matched in order; the LAST matching pattern wins.
# Owners can be GitHub usernames (@user), team handles (@org/team-name),
# or email addresses.
#
# Tips:
#   - Put broad fallback rules first, narrow overrides last.
#   - GitHub auto-requests review from the matching owner on every PR
#     touching the matched paths. Combine with branch protection's
#     "Require review from Code Owners" for enforcement.
#   - Keep the file short. If you find yourself maintaining a per-folder
#     map for every directory, the codebase is probably already over-owned.

# --- Default owner for everything not matched below ---
*                       @<DEFAULT_OWNER>

# --- Documentation ---
# /README.md             @<DOCS_OWNER>
# /CLAUDE.md             @<DOCS_OWNER>
# /docs/                 @<DOCS_OWNER>

# --- CI / build / dependency configuration ---
# /.github/              @<INFRA_OWNER>
# /.github/workflows/    @<INFRA_OWNER>
# /.github/dependabot.yml @<INFRA_OWNER>

# --- Security-sensitive areas ---
# /.github/SECURITY.md   @<SECURITY_OWNER>
# /.well-known/          @<SECURITY_OWNER>
# /sw.js                 @<SECURITY_OWNER>
# /service-worker.js     @<SECURITY_OWNER>
# /manifest.json         @<SECURITY_OWNER>
# /manifest.webmanifest  @<SECURITY_OWNER>

# --- Per-language / per-module overrides (uncomment as needed) ---
# *.py                   @<PYTHON_OWNER>
# *.kt                   @<ANDROID_OWNER>
# /web/                  @<FRONTEND_OWNER>
# /server/               @<BACKEND_OWNER>
